[Music]  robert downey jr's career may have  reached astronomical heights when he was  cast as tony stark aka iron man in the  very first film of the marvel cinematic  universe but he already had a long  career before that with a ton of ups and  downs so you might be surprised to find  out that he doesn't consider his best  film to be iron man or any of his marvel  blockbuster appearances downey started  out doing roles in 80s comedies like  weird science and then proved his  dramatic acting chops in less than zero  in the 90s downey's film credits were a  bit hit or miss on the one hand he  received an oscar nomination for his  portrayal of charlie chaplin in the  biopic chaplain and his starring role in  the 1995 historical drama restoration  was well received by critics plus he had  a recurring role on the hit tv series  ally mcbeal on the other hand movies  like the sappy rom-com hearts and souls  and the underwhelming thriller in dreams  weren't a big help in moving his career  forward and after a serious drug  addiction derailed his career in the  late 90s and early 2000s downey jr  struggled to find work as few people in  hollywood were willing to take a risk on  him that may be one reason why during a  2020 appearance on the joe rogan  experience podcast downey jr said that  his best film was also the one that had  the most importance to his career kiss  kiss bang bang released in 2005 kiss  kiss bang bang is an action-packed dark  comedy produced by downey's friend joel  silver downey told rogan that it was  quote in some ways the best film i've  ever done it came out and it bombed but  john favreau saw it and he said this guy  could do an action movie that wound up  being my calling card into the marvel  universe john favreau of course directed  and co-starred in iron man in 2008 and  he gave downey jr his next big launch  into stardom and though kiss kiss bang  bang only made 15.7 million dollars  worldwide at the box office it was a big  hit with critics with a certified fresh  score of 86 percent on rotten tomatoes  to go along with an audience score of 87  percent kiss kiss bang bang was also  written and directed by shane black who  downey later brought in to write and  direct iron man 3 after fabro bowed out  of the franchise like downey black was  also in a career slump before kiss kiss  bang bang the writer director had  previously found great success writing  and producing movies like lethal weapon  and the last boy scout but after the  long kiss goodnight bombed at the box  office in 1996 he struggled to find work  in hollywood kiss kiss bang bang was  black's attempt to start over by  branching out from straight action  movies the fact that he himself had  trouble finding people to take a chance  on him may have influenced his decision  to give downey a second chance as well  thankfully for all of us black took the  risk and hired downey to play one of the  main characters though kiss kiss bang  bang didn't do very well at the box  office it did become a cult classic the  quality of the film helped revive both  black and downey's careers and set the  wheels in motion for marvel to also take  a risk on casting downy in the first  iron man film it's hard to believe now  after downey jr's breakout performances  tony stark set the stage for the marvel  cinematic universe to become the biggest  film franchise in history but when he  was first cast in iron man in 2006 there  were many who were skeptical downey jr  could be trusted with the responsibility  his work on kiss kiss bang bang was good  enough to convince marvel to take the  chance though and the rest is history no  wonder downey thinks it's his best film  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

